What must be enforced in code
At session admission: no agent starts protected estate work without authenticated identity, a valid capability contract and inherited failure-class controls.
At task admission: every accepted instruction is persisted atomically with an accountable owner. A message or GitHub comment is not a task acceptance receipt.
At delegation: only authorized workers with matching capabilities can acquire fenced, expiring leases.
At tool execution: protected effects require fresh authorization, correct scope, idempotency and a valid lease. Direct bypass routes must be removed or independently guarded.
At completion: a process exit, ACK, passing unit test or agent declaration cannot produce VERIFIED_EFFECT.
At recovery: expired leases, disconnected workers and unacknowledged obligations trigger bounded reconciliation and reassignment.
At evolution: contract changes invalidate affected proofs and require compatibility checks before promotion.
The enforcement must reuse existing capability-index, registry-gate, QUAD, FLOW, Legion, Temporal, KARMA and the policy infrastructure already specified in the estate. No second registry or orchestration engine.

