4. How we actually force agents to comply
Enforcement point A — Agent bootstrap

The shared admission mechanism refuses protected work when discovery, context, identity or contract attestations are missing. Every provider adapter must invoke it. Sessions that cannot establish these prerequisites receive a structured BLOCKED_ADMISSION result.

Enforcement point B — Communications gateway

Transport messages are authenticated, persisted and correlated with FLOW obligations. Distinguish DELIVERED, ACCEPTED, CLAIMED, EXECUTED and VERIFIED. The existing estate-fleet ACK semantics must be corrected.

Enforcement point C — Collaboration scheduler

Before taking protected work, the agent must check for an existing owner, compatible specialist, reusable implementation and outstanding dependency. Legion owns capability matching and delegation; Temporal/FLOW owns durable execution and recovery.

Enforcement point D — Actual effect doors

GitHub mutations, deployments, infrastructure changes, credentials and other protected effects require scoped authority and valid execution receipts. Agent instructions alone cannot prevent bypass; underlying credentials and routes must enforce it.

Enforcement point E — Independent finality

No agent can certify its own outcome. Only an authorized verifier can transition a task to VERIFIED_EFFECT, using externally checked evidence and the task’s declared postconditions.

